{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/38710-what-can-you-tell-me-about-the-idigam","id":38710,"title":"What can you tell me about the Idigam?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-29T06:56:47-08:00","id":38710,"title":"What can you tell me about the Idigam?","content":"So, at this point WW:tF is one of two NWoD core books I don't own, and I've at least gotten to read through a friend's copy of M:tAw. I was going to order a copy of Forsaken, but since it's not available PoD, I figured at this point I'd just wait for Idigam Chronicle since it's a stand alone update source book (say that five times fast) anyway.<br /> <br /> But basically all I know is that Idigam are really powerful spirits. That's it. Maybe very alien spirits? Not sure. Something in passing at one point about the Crypt of the Butterfly on the Dark side of the moon? <br /> <br /> (Side question: Has the whole Crypt of the Butterfly thing been explored beyond passing references? I mean has it actually been given a full treatment in an adventure/SAS?)<br /> <br /> <br /> So what can you tell me/what do I need to know to prepare me for the Idigam Chronicle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T10:36:35-08:00","id":38785,"title":"","content":"The idigam are detailed in the great Night Horrors: Wolfsbane book.<br /> <br /> Father Wolf was once a powerful spirit that kind of patrolled the World and kept all the troublemaking spirits from troublemaking. This usually involved killing them or imprisoning them or shattering them. But the idigam couldn't be killed, imprisoned or shattered. Whatever Father Wolf did, they just adapted. So he grabbed them up and tossed them onto the moon, where they've been ever since (it's possible he missed a couple), until humans landed on the moon and they, hungry for material to work with, hitched a ride back to earth.<br /> <br /> They don't have a reflection in the real world. They aren't cat spirits, they're something wild and crazy (made more crazy by their isolation on the moon) and they want to do things. I've heard theories that they are spirits of things that once existed, but no longer do, but generally they're portrayed as unique. Some of them are world-ending threats, some of them are likely to leave the world alone except for a few it chooses as prey. Even their abilities are weird, one of them can simply pluck souls from people and shove spirits inside them, instantly making spirit-claimed.<br /> <br /> As far as I know, it's unrelated to the Crypt of the Butterfly, except for the &quot;things being kept on the moon,&quot; bit. That said, the crypt has a write-up in the God Machine Chronicles as one of the optional stories.<br /> <br /> All that said, if Blood and Smoke is anything to go by it's entirely likely they'll change a bit when Idigam Chronicles comes out.<br /> <br /> tl;dr really powerful, really crazy, really weird spirits","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-29-2013, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T17:31:26-08:00","id":39706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/38710-what-can-you-tell-me-about-the-idigam?p=38785#post38785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't have a reflection in the real world. They aren't cat spirits, they're something wild and crazy (made more crazy by their isolation on the moon) and they want to do things. I've heard theories that they are spirits of things that once existed, but no longer do, but generally they're portrayed as unique. Some of them are world-ending threats, some of them are likely to leave the world alone except for a few it chooses as prey. Even their abilities are weird, one of them can simply pluck souls from people and shove spirits inside them, instantly making spirit-claimed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always wondered about various agendas that Idigam have. One clearly wants to take over the world. Another one simply wants to stop change (and as a result, has taken over a church) while another clearly wants to play Genius: The Transgression with SCIENCE!.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T10:00:39-08:00","id":62267,"title":"","content":"The idigam have their own weird purposes, but one thing to remember when considering their bans (if you were gonna craft one), their ban usually has something to do with where they coalesced. Example: The breeder is all about getting Uratha to bang it out so that they can make unihar, so it can find a potential mate in a powerful spirit. Scary enough of a concept. How to kill it? It's ban is the blood that comes from an uratha giving birth to an unihar. That's right, all that blood that fills the womb instead of a flesh baby. How in the hell is anyone gonna figure that out? And then assuming spirits told you that (i imagine the Hisil is not fond of unihar as a whole), what werewolf wants to take the harmony violation to birth THAT?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T10:50:39-08:00","id":62304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/38710-what-can-you-tell-me-about-the-idigam?p=62267#post62267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idigam have their own weird purposes, but one thing to remember when considering their bans (if you were gonna craft one), their ban usually has something to do with where they coalesced. Example: The breeder is all about getting Uratha to bang it out so that they can make unihar, so it can find a potential mate in a powerful spirit. Scary enough of a concept. How to kill it? It's ban is the blood that comes from an uratha giving birth to an unihar. That's right, all that blood that fills the womb instead of a flesh baby. How in the hell is anyone gonna figure that out? And then assuming spirits told you that (i imagine the Hisil is not fond of unihar as a whole), what werewolf wants to take the harmony violation to birth THAT?</div> </div> </div> </div>I really wanted to like W:tF more than I did, but every now and then I saw stuff like this in the book and was floored by how flavorful it could be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T10:58:23-08:00","id":62317,"title":"","content":"Tis the horror aspect. I liken classic world to Resident evil where as new world is Silent Hill. Ones creepy but fun in a violence manner. One is oppressively disturbing. Another fun analogy would be some aspects of the Hisil could be like stuff from a Clive Barker novel. I personally like it, but it adds such an insane challenge... not that idigam are to be easy mind you. I think that's the terrorizing part. On another note, anyone think the lady in the lake for lodge of the lake is an Idigam? Or is it just an aspect of Maeljin?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}